WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:06.100
I will never let her be scared again. Never!

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.980
We will live in peace until the end of eternity!

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.150
And anybody who gets in our way will die!

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.950
No way! I connected with you?

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.930
Time travel... We've gone to the past!

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:15.640
Yayoi-san?

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:25.600
<i>March 10th, just after midnight, approximately 130 B-29 bombers attacked the capital in force,</i>

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:30.120
<i>dropping bombs indiscriminately citywide for two hours and forty minutes.</i>

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.700
An attack on the capital?

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.910
<i>This haphazard bombing sparked fires...</i>

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.990
The 10th of what year?

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.250
Yayoi-san!

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.660
You're the only person here I can rely on, Yayoi-san!

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.120
No.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.460
I know it hurts, but we need to do something about this first.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.190
Hey, Yayoi-san.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.280
Are you OK?

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.670
She fainted...

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.620
What should I do? Just stay here?

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.670
This is probably the time in which Yayoi-san lived,

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:07.490
which means that all students should be conscripted for factory work.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.450
Guess I'll check it out.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.230
If the factories are too far, I lose.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.630
If the military police catch me, I lose.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.640
But if I find this era's Arashi-san,
I may be able to work something out.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.740
I'll make it back to the future, Arashi-san!

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.250
Natsu no Arashi!
The World Exists for Us Two
Yayoi

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.520
OK! Got it!

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.030
It doesn't seem like that brutal of a time.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.560
Actually, it seems kind of familiar.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.000
What is she so scared of?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.130
Oh, Yayoi-chan!

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:53.290
Why the wheelchair?
Did something happen at the factories?

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.680
Oh crap! She knows Yayoi-san!

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.380
Are you OK, miss?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.940
She was in a little accident.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.140
My, that's awful.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:09.690
Anyway, I'd like to go to the labor factory.
Do you know the way?

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.560
I'm new here.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.470
Oh, you just make a right, up there.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.390
Hurry...

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.300
And run.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:59.370
There are massive bombings on April 15th and May 29th!

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.390
Hey!

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:01.530
Yayoi-chan?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.640
This whole place will be burned to the ground, just like Tokyo!

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.750
So... So...

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:11.040
Yayoi-chan, don't say things like that.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:16.600
If the secret police hear you,
your whole family will be in danger.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.550
But it's true.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:19.920
Thank you.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.360
I'll remember that.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.250
Take care of your legs.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.510
She doesn't believe you?

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.890
Of course not...

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.530
We're from the future, and...

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.410
How can you explain that?

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:42.160
It won't always work out like it did with Arashi-san. I knew that, but...

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:45.070
You can't change some things, even if you know about them.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:48.790
Yeah. They're all going to burn in the bombings.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.330
Run... Run away...

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.530
Yayoi-san?

00:05:55.700 --> 00:06:00.010
Even now, she's trying to help others.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:05.120
How great must the terror carved into her soul be?

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.120
That's the factory.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.390
The inside is classified and off-limits, I bet.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:14.110
I'll just have to walk around the perimeter and look for Arashi-san.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.970
I guess I'll rest a bit.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:20.220
I don't think anyone will come here.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.720
Kanako!

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:30.010
Oh, Yayoi-san! You're awake?

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.420
Who are you?

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:36.620
Brother! It's you, Brother!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.760
I'm so happy to see you here.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.170
I guess, even when you're dead, good things do happen.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.280
Yayoi-san, what happened to you guys?

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.970
What happened?

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.740
I don't remember.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:54.370
When I woke up, I was with Kanako.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:59.010
I must've lost the use of my legs in the bombings.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:04.950
I can't walk, but Kanako takes care of me.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:07.230
You're close friends, huh?

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.000
Yeah!

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.530
Kanako's so kind and smart.

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:15.100
We're like ghosts now.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.440
At first, we didn't really know what to do.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.970
But we talk and cheer each other up,

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.310
and somehow, we've managed to accept it.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.210
We've lived each summer in peace.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:31.470
A quiet time, without any war.

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:44.430
Kanako?

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.700
What is it, Yayoi?

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.650
Time's passing in the outside world, isn't it?

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:53.290
Yes... We can only live during the summer, after all.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.730
It kind of bothers me.

00:07:55.730 --> 00:08:03.760
I love summer because it overflows with life,
but I'd also like to feel fall, winter, and spring.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:11.800
What do those who survived the bombing feel,
living out the rest of their lives?

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:15.620
Yayoi, don't say another word.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:20.010
Your friends and family...
If you knew about them, you'd only suffer.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:27.420
But you're right. I'm sure they're each living their life as best they can.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.760
With a strong will that won't yield to anything.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:37.490
By a whim of God, we were granted a completely different way of life.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:44.570
We mustn't forget who we are.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:48.580
Kanako, let's go see the sea tomorrow.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:50.490
It's hot. Are you OK to do that?

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:51.320
Yeah.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:54.090
As long as I have your special iced tea.

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:57.190
I'll make a big batch for us to take.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:58.810
All right!

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:01.940
The summers felt like a dream.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.560
And yet...

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.510
It was awful...

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:08.310
God was so awful. He was playing with our lives.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.680
Yayoi?

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:14.910
What should I do?

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:18.280
The piano... I can't play the piano!

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.330
Yayoi?

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.490
It's OK.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:27.960
It's OK, Kanako.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:33.100
I'm sure it's a sign from God that we've lived long enough.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:37.270
The sixty summers you spent together...

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:42.690
I don't yet understand what tied you together so tightly.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.210
But...

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:46.370
Don't worry.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:52.700
I'll... I'll find a way to keep us from disappearing.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.640
What are you doing?

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.580
You again?

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:59.010
What are you thinking, Fushimi-san?

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:00.350
It's the Kanako from the past?

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:05.670
Stop showing up all the time!
This place is supposed to be mine alone!

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:08.170
But we promised.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.780
If something happened, we'd meet here.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:12.180
Don't screw with me!

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:13.900
Kanako? You're mad?

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.470
I don't know what kind of act you're pulling,

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:20.750
but if you've got time to screw around that way, you're every bit the spoiled brat I thought.

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:21.810
Kanako?

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:23.890
How long do you plan on messing with me?

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.640
I'm really getting sick of it!

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:26.880
Stop it, Kanako!

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:28.310
Shut up!

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:32.290
I've had to work for months,
for years, all for people like you!

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:36.730
Everything my family owned was taken to benefit the 0.5 percent of this country who are rich!

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:39.060
I... I...

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:43.390
Get down!

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:53.090
A US plane?

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.670
A fighter attack from that range?

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.880
They're after us!

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:01.700
It's coming back around!

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:09.960
That's Kanako.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:10.890
Yayoi-san...

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:12.860
Kanako...

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.190
Kanako! Kanako!

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.740
Kanako!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.590
Just a few minutes ago, I said I'd help her.

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:48.400
And I couldn't even move.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.570
Yayoi-san!

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.800
Yayoi-san...

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:13.150
She's alive.

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.450
The fear of death...

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:19.980
The regret and self-hatred at my inability
to take even one step...

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.130
But even so, what could I have done?

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:29.660
The fact that they were safe broke my repetitious chain of thought.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:31.630
I'm alive...

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:34.590
Yayoi-san put herself in harm's way for you.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:39.910
I'm glad.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.170
H-Hey...

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.330
I'm leaving.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:49.020
Are you OK by yourself?

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:51.460
I'm fine!

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.620
Man, she's such a bitch.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:12:59.740
Anyway!

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.310
Yayoi-san, your legs!

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:03.750
Stand up.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:05.380
Come on.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:16.520
I can stand...

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.920
I can walk! I can walk!

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:22.730
Why?

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:23.980
I can't believe it!

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:27.150
Your other emotions conquered your fears.

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:36.490
Yayoi-san!

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:37.840
You still shouldn't-

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.780
When we get back, Kanako will be happy

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:46.010
that something so wonderful could happen.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.220
Yayoi-san.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.770
Oh, yes. You want to meet Arashi, right?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.110
Yes, I only want a glimpse of her.

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:07.260
I guess guys from every era fall in love with Arashi-san.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.780
That's not it! That's not how it is!

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:15.650
She's really helped me out. I want to see what she's like in this time.

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:19.460
Oh, I see. Huh?

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.530
She's not working at the factory.

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:23.780
Maybe today is...

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:25.990
You have some idea?

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:27.160
Yayoi-san!

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:35.320
Good afternoon.

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:37.830
Good luck with the piano at the concert today.

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:39.600
Ah, right.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:42.290
Who's that?

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:43.350
An acquaintance?

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:49.990
Yes, a relative. H-He came to hear me play today.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:52.570
He's certainly a stylish guy.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:54.140
Do I know you?

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.950
It's strange. I feel like this isn't the first time I've met you.

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:02.770
Arashi, that's inappropriate.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:05.170
Sorry, sorry.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.480
See you later, Yayoi-san.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:08.300
Right!

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:14.460
N-Non-ghost Arashi is pretty awesome, too!

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:17.000
Today, the power's off. I knew it!

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.220
The day of the concert!

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:23.830
Yayoi-san, is it the one where Arashi-san and Kaya-san sing?

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:24.980
Yes, that's it.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.450
I want to see it!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:27.740
Let's go.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.840
You go by yourself.

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:35.330
I shouldn't go. I'd meet the version of myself in this time.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.520
But...

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:41.280
This is an important day to Kanako and me.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:46.740
If it weren't for this day,
we'd never have been friends.

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:48.080
Seriously?

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.310
Yes.

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:52.490
So, I want you to see it for yourself.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.590
I'm going to wait on that hill.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.120
It's fine.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.890
More than enough amazing things have already happened to me.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.850
All right!

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.950
He does like her.

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:09.860
Here?

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.500
Is it gonna start?

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:23.560
Everyone, thank you for gathering here today.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:27.550
I don't know how much longer we'll be able to have concerts like this,

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:30.840
but I'll sing my best, so please enjoy it.

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:34.420
Yayoi-san?

00:16:49.820 --> 00:17:02.990
<i>They call it spring, but the wind is quite cold.</i>

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:18.330
<i>The nightingale of the valley wants to sing,</i>

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:18.200
Bright, strong, and filled with warmth,

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:24.510
her voice held no darkness at all, even in the darkness of wartime.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:32.530
<i>but knows it is not time, and does not.</i>

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:29.150
Arashi's voice enveloped all who heard it.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:33.840
On the other hand, Kaya-san's voice held a touch of sadness.

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:45.040
<i>But knows it is not time, and does not.</i>

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:38.200
And yet, you could feel a strong will resound in the depths of your heart.

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:45.020
Is Yayoi-san worried about Kanako?

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.830
She seems kind of depressed.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.950
Damn it. What is Kanako doing...

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.440
There she is!

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.980
Kanako, what are you doing?
Get in here!

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:55.540
Jeez...

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:59.330
Kanako, you're late!

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:01.500
Yamazaki-san?

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.730
Yamazaki-san is here.

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:15.260
<i>The ice melts and fades away,
the reed beds begin to sprout,</i>

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:04.050
That's odd.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:29.480
<i>and when it's thought to be time, everything
springs back with anticipation.</i>

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:31.480
<i>The snow continues to fall...</i>

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:38.260
That was wonderful.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.770
I think I'm in love.

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:42.410
I hope another blackout day comes soon.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.340
Arashi-san is great.

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:46.310
I'm even more in love.

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:52.890
Thank you for that.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:57.230
So, uh...

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:02.090
I'm sorry for what I said about you.

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:05.200
I guess I'm still just a kid.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.110
No, I'm...

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:13.200
Um, if you want...
Would you like to talk after this?

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:18.870
Y-Yeah. I guess so.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:19.900
Great!

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:21.720
Um, thanks!

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:28.520
I see. So that was it.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.330
How was it, Yasaka-kun?

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:35.520
It was a wonderful song and performance.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.610
Thank you.

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:39.700
Yayoi-san, I figured it out.

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.340
The reason she came to your concert.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.060
Huh?

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:46.660
It was because you'd gone and saved her.

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:52.820
She said those horrible things to you, but you saved her, risking your life.

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:56.950
It's possible that she would've died in the attack today.

00:19:56.950 --> 00:20:01.640
But you saved her, and that changed history to what was meant to be.

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:07.400
So Yayoi-san, your friendship with Kanako was something you created.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:11.980
Yayoi!

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:14.600
Yayoi!

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:16.110
Kanako.

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.000
Why are you here?

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.490
No way. You connected with Shades?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:22.330
This is impossible.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:23.390
This is a dream!

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.690
Yayoi, your legs...

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:28.510
Yup.

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:31.630
Look at this. I can walk.

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:35.350
I can help you from now on.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:37.720
I'm sorry to make you worry.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:40.050
And thank you, Kanako.

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:45.150
Let's go back.

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:47.140
I did what I had to.

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:49.100
Yayoi...

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:52.340
There was a purpose to these bodies of ours.

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:55.350
A very important one...

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:59.600
Now that I've done what I had to,
I've never been so happy.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.850
So I'm fine.

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:04.180
No matter what happens to us,

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.150
I'm fine.

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:07.660
I see.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:09.300
Yes, I understand.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.340
We're going back.

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:15.510
Yes.

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:55.630
Bored...

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:58.540
Anything interesting to talk about?

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:00.500
Um...

00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:03.760
I read a book a while ago.

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:06.320
What was it called?

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:09.610
Well, I forgot the title.

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:12.320
Tell me what kind of story it was.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:13.390
Yes.

00:23:13.390 --> 00:23:15.520
Wait a second. I'll remember it.

00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:20.090
It was the story of a terrifying gir-

00:23:20.090 --> 00:23:21.470
Glass Mask!

00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:26.580
Arashi!

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:27.600
Arashi-san!

00:23:27.600 --> 00:23:29.920
Arashi is a terrifying girl!

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:32.490
When you think of summer, you think of-

00:23:32.490 --> 00:23:33.510
Camping!

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:35.680
And campfires at night!

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:37.230
Roasting marshmallows on an open fire.

00:23:37.230 --> 00:23:39.810
You put them with chocolate, between crackers.

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:41.140
That sounds good!

00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:44.180
Get up bright and early tomorrow!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.200
<i>Get up bright and early tomorrow!</i>

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.200
Illustration by Kantoku
